  "result_text": "The median order value in June is **$76.36**. That figure covers only June 1\u201314, because the file stops there.\n\n- **What I computed:** the median `amount` across all 268 orders in `orders.csv`. Every row is dated in June, and there are no blank amounts, no duplicate order IDs and no unparseable timestamps.\n- **Coverage:** the file has orders for June 1 through June 14 only, 17 to 23 per day. Nothing exists for June 15\u201330. I can't tell from the file whether the rest of the month was never exported or whether there were no orders. If you meant the full month, this number could shift once the second half is included.\n- **Currency:** I assumed the `amount` column is in a single currency. The file doesn't state one.\n- **Client version:** the medians for the two client versions are close: 74.52 for 3.4.0 (168 orders) and 76.95 for 3.4.1 (100 orders). Nothing suggests the amounts differ in units or definition between them.\n\nNo working files were needed for this, so nothing was written to the work directory."
